AB  - Cacao farming is crucial for tropical economies, including the Philippines, but is threatened by diseases like black pod rot (caused by Phytophthora palmivora ), causing economic losses. This scoping review examines AI-based models for detecting black pod rot, evaluating their effectiveness in identifying infection symptoms. It consolidates performance metrics, identifies model limitations, and explores future research opportunities. The findings highlight AI’s potential for improving disease management, boosting yields, and promoting sustainability in cacao farming, ultimately enhancing productivity and economic stability for farmers despite existing challenges.
